{"conversation_id":"59297e90-c75b-4bb0-a9b0-efa27eff104f","response":"A fascinating topic! Climate change is having significant impacts on polar bear habitats. According to a 2019 study published in the journal Nature Climate Change by Laidre et al., the reduction of sea ice coverage is directly threatening polar bear survival (DOI: 10.1038/s41558-019-0533-6).

The study demonstrated that polar bears require stable sea ice platforms for hunting and breeding. With Arctic sea ice declining at approximately 13% per decade, these animals are facing critical habitat loss. Cited research by Amstrup et al. (2017) in the journal Global Change Biology further underscores the alarming rate of habitat reduction (DOI: 10.1111/gcb.13678).

Would you like more detailed information or specific research findings? I can certainly provide additional academic sources to support these observations."}

